---
import { PLAN, formatNumber } from "../../lib/site";
import Screenshot from "../Screenshot.astro";
---

<section id="features" aria-labelledby="ranking-title" class="py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="container-page grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="text-eyebrow">AI ranking</p>
      <h2 id="ranking-title" class="text-heading mt-4">A match score you can actually read.</h2>
      <p class="text-lead mt-6">
        Every application is scored against the job as soon as it arrives. Instead of a mystery number, you see
        how each applicant measures up on the things that matter for the role.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">A clear breakdown.</strong> Skills, experience, seniority fit, and
          qualifications are each scored, so you can see exactly where someone stands out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">More than a resume.</strong> Answers to your application questions are
          part of the picture too.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Fair and consistent.</strong> Every applicant for a job is scored the
          same way, against the same criteria.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">You stay in charge.</strong> The match is there to guide your review, not
          replace it. Update a job, and you can rank its applicants again.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <figure class="rounded-3xl bg-subtle p-5 ring-1 ring-line sm:p-8">
        <div class="shot">
          <Screenshot
            name="match"
            alt="An applicant's 91% match in Emploist, broken down into skills (93), experience (88), seniority fit (95), and qualifications (85), each with a short explanation."
            sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 40rem, (min-width: 64rem) 52vw, calc(100vw - 5rem)"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-5 text-sm text-faint sm:mt-6">
          Each ranking uses one AI credit. Your plan comes with {formatNumber(PLAN.credits)} every month.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
